    {
      "body": "@njhill Updated to use Model Runner V2 as requested. I traced the V2 no-draft path and found that it already avoids the reported MRV1 bug: it sets expanded_idx_mapping equal to idx_mapping, so each request owns one logits row and ThinkingBudgetState applies forcing through that explicit mapping. I removed the MRV1 implementation change and its five MRV1 tests, then replaced them with a two-request V2 GPU regression test that asserts both exhausted budgets force their own rows on a draft-less speculative step. There is intentionally no V2 implementation change because the supported path is already correct; the updated PR now protects that invariant without claiming a nonexistent V2 bug.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-10T03:37:55Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/59291#issuecomment-6093376610",
      "id": 6093376610,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-10T03:37:55Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Kylinny"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @njhill — following up on your suggestion to use the V2 model runner: this PR is now a regression test for the draftless thinking-budget row mapping (I traced the V2 no-draft path and confirmed it already avoids the row-overlap this test guards). DCO is green. Whenever you have a moment, I would appreciate a re-review — happy to adjust anything. Thanks!",
